      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>First off, welcome to the forums, hope you survive the experience.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As to your question, all damage done has a type but the type itself has no different effect on a villain, it is just an idea of how the hero is dealing damage (e.g. Tachyon does Melee damage because she punches people really fast). But some ongoing/equipment cards can increase or decrease specific types of damage, or certain targets can be immune to specific types of damage, it&#39;s all detailed on the cards themselves.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If you look at Wraith&#39;s deck you can find a card called &quot;Micro targeting computers&quot; which increase any projectile damage she does, if you were to play a oneshot card does melee damage then Microt argeting computers will not increase the damage done but most of Wraith&#39;s powers do Projectile damage so that damage would be increased.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Another card you might want to look at is Ra&#39;s &quot;Flesh of the sun god&quot;, it makes him immune to Fire damage, so he would ignore any Fire damage but all other types of damage would still reduce his HP normally.</p>",
